From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christophe Chapuis <chris.chapuis@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Jun 2021 16:15:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] service: order after android-system and wifi-module-load

On LuneOS the Android side is brought up by android-system.service rather than
droid-hal-init.service, and on tissot-halium the Bluetooth firmware only becomes
reachable once the WiFi module has been loaded (both share the same combo chip),
so bluebinder has to start after wifi-module-load.service as well.

Rebased for 1.0.20: upstream reworked the unit in fecaa79/eacf61f (Type=notify,
ExecStartPre/Post, sandboxing) and renamed the ordering dependency from
android-system.service to droid-hal-init.service.

Signed-off-by: Christophe Chapuis <chris.chapuis@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [LuneOS-specific service naming]
---
 bluebinder.service | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/bluebinder.service b/bluebinder.service
index a9f6c56..2296e51 100644
--- a/bluebinder.service
+++ b/bluebinder.service
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 [Unit]
 Description=Simple proxy for using android binder based bluetooth through vhci.
-After=droid-hal-init.service
+After=android-system.service wifi-module-load.service
 Before=bluetooth.service

 [Service]
--
2.34.1
